  "notes": "Official cause_code/category are 'TBD'/'provisional' per FORM-366 fields; narrative attributes the root cause to inadequate turbine trip logic design not accounting for MSR pressure transients during load rejection testing. No SSCs were inoperable at event onset; operators and RPS functioned as designed, so no BACKED_UP_BY edges were warranted (steam generator PORVs were used for decay heat removal post-trip, modeled as a component involved in mitigation rather than a backup system per rule 6, since PORVs are normal post-trip heat removal path, not a stated operable backup to a failed system). Previous Similar Events section states 'None', so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge emitted per rule 9 (only applicable when a previous occurrence is actually referenced)."
